  "description": "The reusable phasor-model engine: define a model, train it data-parallel through an EvalApp pipeline, and run inference (predict / generate, with an optional KV cache). Ships two param-for-param comparable cores — AlgFormer (softmax dot-product attention) and HoloFormer (holographic-native attention: bind the key to its value, causally bundle into one superposed memory trace, then resonate the query to retrieve, O(T·d) with O(1) KV-serve) — plus HoloShape capacity-law sizing, compute-equivalent (invisible-param) accounting, a built-in subword tokenizer, checkpoint save/load with in-place growth (context/shifts/vocabulary), and MQTT-based distributed/swarm training. HoloFormer also ships an opt-in, default-OFF per-layer Adam gate (\"ADAM & EVE\") that nudges a layer's update toward a codebook-derived target norm range; default off and byte-identical when unused, but live in production via the GPU-fused trainer (see AlgFormer.Gpu) since 2026-09-24. Pure double[] + SIMD, no external ML runtime. Built on the Phasor VSA codec and the EvalApp pipeline runtime.",
